Using Convex 1.44.0, messages has author: string, text: string, likes: number, isPinned: boolean and .index("by_author", ["author"]). A query validates { author: string, minLikes: number }. All of that author’s messages fit within query limits. It must load all of those messages and apply the pinned and likes checks in JavaScript. The handler is:

```ts
const authorQuery = ctx.db.query("messages")
  .withIndex("by_author", (q) => q.eq("author", args.author));
// Insert one option here.
return selected.sort((a, b) => b.likes - a.likes);
```

